## Original Content
<p style="text-align: center;"><img alt="当地时间4日凌晨，李在明支持者们聚集在国会前等待计票结果。人民网 柳美铉摄" height="451" src="/NMediaFile/2025/0604/MAIN1748998400707PSHWTVD4SV.jpg" width="800" /></p> <p style="text-align: center;"><span>当地时间4日凌晨，李在明支持者们聚集在国会前等待计票结果。人民网 柳美铉摄</span></p> <p style="text-indent: 2em;">人民网首尔6月4日电 （周玉波、李美玉） 韩国中央选举管理委员会6月4日通过大选计票结果，正式确认共同民主党候选人李在明当选第21届韩国总统，李在明的总统任期自当地时间4日6时21分正式开启。</p> <p style="text-indent: 2em;">韩国中央选举委员会于当地时间4日7时10分左右向第21届总统大选当选人李在明的代理人、共同民主党党鞭朴赞大颁发当选证。</p> <p style="text-indent: 2em;">4日凌晨，在大选计票期间，李在明来到位于首尔汝矣岛的国会前发表讲话，对国民表示感谢。李在明表示，将全力以赴重振经济、恢复民生对话沟通。他还表示，将通过朝韩对话，寻求共存及共同繁荣之路。</p> <p style="text-indent: 2em;">韩国行政安全部表示，第21届总统李在明的宣誓就职仪式将于当地时间4日11时在国会举行。</p> <p style="text-indent: 2em;">根据计票结果，共同民主党候选人李在明的得票率为49.42%（1728.75万张），国民力量党候选人金文洙和改革新党候选人李俊锡的得票率分别为41.15%和8.34%。</p> <p style="text-indent: 2em;">本届选举是韩国自1987年宪政改革以来第二次在总统缺位情况下选举总统，当选总统无交接期，在选举结果正式确定后立即履职。</p>

## Summary
Lee Jae-myung has been elected as the 21st President of South Korea with 49.42% of the votes, and his presidency begins immediately without a transition period due to the absence of an outgoing president. He expressed gratitude to supporters and outlined plans to focus on economic recovery, public dialogue, and inter-Korean cooperation. The election is significant as it marks the second time since 1987 that a president is elected in such circumstances.

## Key Points
- Lee Jae-myung wins the presidential election with 49.42% of the vote, defeating opponents Kim Moon-soo (41.15%) and Lee Jun-seok (8.34%).
- The presidential term starts immediately after election results, without a transition period, as it's an election held without an incumbent president.
- Lee Jae-myung emphasizes priorities such as reviving the economy, restoring public dialogue, and engaging in inter-Korean talks for mutual prosperity.
- The Central Election Management Committee certified the results, and the inauguration ceremony is scheduled for the same day.
- This election is historically notable in South Korea, being the second such event since the 1987 constitutional reforms.


